        "category": "engine",
        "title": "Early F87 M2 Boost-Control Software Faults",
        "description": "BMW SIB 12 17 16 defines an F87 M2 path for vehicles produced through August 3, 2016 when a Drivetrain Malfunction message, reduced power and DME faults 120208 and 120408 occur. BMW identifies an overly sensitive DME diagnostic threshold that can switch off turbocharging-pressure control. The bulletin does not establish a cracked plastic charge pipe.",
        "solution": "Read the DME faults with the current BMW ISTA version and confirm the production date. If the vehicle meets SIB 12 17 16, program the vehicle to integration level F020-16-07-504 or higher. Do not replace a charge pipe from this card. ShowMeTheParts resolves exact 2016 M2 turbocharger and 3.0-liter fitment but returned no charge-pipe candidate; even a catalog match would not prove the BMW software fault or repair role.",
        "severity": "medium",
        "confidence": "high",
